#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# same

#% text
# `same(a, b)`, written `a === b`, gives `true` when the two terms are identical, else `false`; it never stays unevaluated.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It compares structure, not value: `1` and `1.0` are different terms.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
same(x + 1, 1 + x)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
1 === 1.0
#% output
#= false

#% cell
same(x, y)
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Compare with `==`, which compares values and can stay symbolic:

#% cell
[1 == 1.0, x == y]
#% output
#= [true, x == y]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `not_same`, `equal`, `match_q`
